WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:09.600
Oh, my gosh, knitting and Intarsia is so
easy with the TH-160. What's in Intarsia ?

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.360
It allows you to knit blocks of color

3
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:18.440
across the row at the same time,
without any floats across the back.

4
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.120
The manual makes this seem really
complicated, but it's not.

5
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.240
Let's get started.

6
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.960
Start by knitting a few
rows in plain knitting.

7
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.560
Just get some stitches on the machine
with your main color.

8
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:39.080
End with the carriage on the right and all
needles are in "B", or working position.

9
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.520
Un-hread the working yarn and just
kind of hold it out of the way.

10
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.320
Set the carriage to PART and pass
the carriage to the left.

11
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.800
Remember, with the PART setting

12
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
and the needles in "B" position,
you can safely free past the carriage.

13
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:03.800
Next position, the needles for in Intarsia.
Still no yarn in the carriage.

14
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.600
Move the change lever to Intarsia
and pass the carriage to the right.

15
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:16.320
This time all the needles are aligned in
"D" position and the latches are open.

16
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.600
The carriage is on the right.

17
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:24.360
Put your working ball of yarn on the floor
in front of you and line up the other

18
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:31.040
colors you'll be using. You'll need
an end of yarn for each color.

19
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.760
I'm going to knit three
colors across the row.

20
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.040
I'm sure you will get much
more creative with this.

21
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.320
But for now, let's keep things simple.

22
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:47.080
First place the working yarn
over the first group of needles.

23
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.520
Just lay it on the needles
from right to left.

24
00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.760
Lay the second yarn across
the next set of needles.

25
00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.920
Make sure the tail of the yarn is

26
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:04.640
on the right and the working end is
always going to be away from the carriage.

27
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.160
Lay the third yarn across the last set

28
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.040
of needles. Again, make sure
that tail is on the right.

29
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.760
Don't secure the yarns,

30
00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:20.560
just loosely hold them in your left hand
and pass the carriage to the left.

31
00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:25.680
You'll feel the yarn being fed
into the carriage as the stitches knit.

32
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.440
Now, don't hold too tight.

33
00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.720
Your left hand is now
replacing the tension mast.

34
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.160
Voila.

35
00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:39.320
We've knit all three colors in the row
with one pass of the carriage.

36
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:45.160
The next step is important.
To prevent holes, you need to make sure

37
00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.680
that you cross the yarns as you
position them for the next row.

38
00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:55.720
Lay the blue strand across
the left group of needles.

39
00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.720
Pick up and lay that pink strand
across the center group of needles.

40
00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.760
Notice that the two yarns cross.

41
00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.400
Then lay the green across
the first set of needles.

42
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.600
Holding the three strands
loosely, knit across the row.

43
00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.600
One more time
with the carriage on the right,

44
00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.080
lay the green yarn across
the first group of needles.

45
00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.120
Make sure those yarns cross.

46
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.560
Pick up that pink yarn and lay it across

47
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:38.800
the next group. Cross the yarns and lay
the blue yarn across the needles.

48
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.520
And knit across.

49
00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.760
The change lever stays in Intarsia
for the whole process.

50
00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.040
Because we made sure those yarns crossed,

51
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.920
you can see that the join between
the two colors is secure.

52
00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.240
There aren't any holes

53
00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.720
I'll need to work in all these yarn tails.

54
00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.720
But can you see the possibilities
of this in Intarsia technique?

